<section class="financial-tools">
  <p>Financial Tools</p>

  <h2>Financial Tools</h2>

  <div class="financial-tools-grid">
    <article>
      <h3>Financial Projections</h3>
      <p>
        Financial projections are essential for planning and monitoring a
        company's performance. They provide insights into potential revenue,
        expenses, and profitability over specific periods.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>The Balance Sheet</h3>
      <p>
        The Balance Sheet is a summary of the assets and liabilities and equity
        of a business at a specific point of time.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Income Statement</h3>
      <p>
        The Income (Profit and Loss) Statement, commonly referred to as the
        P&amp;L statement, summarizes the revenue and expenses for a specific
        time period.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Financial Plan</h3>
      <p>
        Keep your information current and review the documents on a regular
        basis (monthly or more often if needed). Review them with key
        individuals within your company.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Financial Ratios</h3>
      <p>
        Ratios are useful when comparing your company with the competition on
        financial performance and also when benchmarking the performance of your
        company.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .financial-tools {
      padding: var(--space-8) 2rem;
    }

    .financial-tools-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }
  }
</style>
